    "prompt": "Use case: game-terrain atlas. Create24 NEW Mindustry obstacle WALL TOP textures. Refined Daoist Q clean bright hand-painted rounded materials from attached references ONLY, no UI/text/characters/symbols/frames. STRICT DIRECTLY TOP-DOWN, no side views. Requested2048×3072 portrait, exactly4 EQUAL columns×6 EQUAL rows,24 square fullbleed opaque cells without gutters or dividers. No global lighting gradient/vignette. Material fills entire square with quiet tileable edges; large rounded connected rock crowns and small soft dark cracks. Each variant has a different native crown/fissure drawing; don't copy.\nRow1 all4 ARKYIC WALL: desaturated blue-teal slate rock with tiny cyan flecks; variants1,2,3 and separate larger 2×2 composition at col4.\nRow2 all4 GRAPHITIC WALL: very dark gray graphite layered rock crowns, restrained silver-gray facets; variants1,2,3 and separate large composition col4.\nRow3 all4 RED STONE WALL: muted terracotta rosy-red rock crowns with thin warm mineral veins; variants1,2,3 and separate large composition col4.\nRow4 all4 CRYSTALLINE STONE WALL: pale violet-gray rock crowns with sparse small lavender crystal facets embedded in cracks; variants1,2,3,4.\nRow5 col1 CRYSTALLINE STONE WALL separate large composition, same material as row4. Col2 DARK METAL WALL variant1, col3 DARK METAL WALL variant2, col4 DARK METAL WALL large design: dark charcoal-jade worn metal obstacle top caps with broad riveted reinforced plates, slight rounded bevels and warm-gold tiny fasteners, no symbols.\nRow6 col1/2/3 RED DIAMOND WALL three distinct large obstacle-top compositions: dense irregular ruby-rose red diamond crystal crowns, chunky faceted crystalline mineral surface, no individually isolated gem. Col4 DARK PANEL4 floor: flat dark charcoal-jade metal lattice ground tile with small round rivets, simple repeated square support grid.\nEach cell complete usable top-down terrain texture, no labels, nothing transparent.",
